"sha256:4553832574145676f9bc08ccc055565131f1411013433a23e39ddf66c50511c7","file":"preprints/The-Bogomolov-Pop-reconstruction-theorem-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":55,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a4f06acb3ac4f9f275cd7d169c964ec28e23c81e2bef6ddc4cca0d9cf825f604","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Bogomolov-Pop-reconstruction-theorem-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4553832574145676f9bc08ccc055565131f1411013433a23e39ddf66c50511c7","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Bogomolov-Pop-reconstruction-theorem-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex#L55"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $k$ and $l$ be arbitrary algebraically closed fields of characteristics\ndifferent from $\\ell$, and let $K/k$ and $L/l$ be function fields with\n$\\trdeg(K/k),\\trdeg(L/l)\\ge2$.  Then\n\\[\n \\Phi_{K,L}:\\Isom_F^i(K,L)\\longrightarrow\n \\Isom^c(\\Pi_L^a,\\Pi_K^a)/\\Zell^\\times,\n \\qquad [\\alpha]\\longmapsto[\\alpha^*],\n\\]\nis a bijection."}
